# Publish a hybrid Rocdown site

Hybrid islands are **experimental**. Static Markdown pages are the stable
Rocdown path. Live pages reuse the application layer; the reserved `@island`
syntax is not implemented.

A hybrid Rocdown site is two artifacts:

1. **CDN tree** — HTML documents, hashed CSS/images, discovery files, and the
   Cmd/Ctrl-K palette (`goto.js`). Pages without handlers do not include
   Datastar. `live` pages include initial island HTML and Datastar.js pointed
   at the island service.
2. **Island service** — `rocdown serve-islands` (colocated handlers) or `rocci run`
   on `[http].service`. Mutation handlers return Datastar patches. The CDN file
   is a snapshot; the service owns durable state.

`docs/` in this repository is a `static` catalog. The public `site/` tree is
hybrid: home is `live` (the SQLite counter island); mounted docs stay
`static`. The worked example is `examples/rocdown/counter`.

See [Rocdown site configuration](/docs/rocdown/sites/) for the field
reference (`service_origin`, `--cdn-only`, `islands.json`).

## Page kinds

| Kind | Meaning | Datastar |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `static` | Markdown / `@page` / `:name[params]` | No |
| `hydrate` | Pure Rocci spliced at build | No |
| `live` | Rocci plus `@get:view` / `@method:fragment` / `@method:command` / `@context` / `@init` or `import Datastar` | Yes |

Apply keeps the `:note` / `:tabs` widget forest on `static` pages. The counter
home page splices island Html; `/about/` has no Datastar. `@render` is not
legal inside a `:note` body.

`rocdown check` accepts all three. Default `rocdown build` accepts `live` and
emits `islands.json`. `rocdown build --cdn-only` errors (`RD2302`) when any
published page is `live`, so a CDN-only publish cannot ship action buttons
with no service.

## Walk the counter

`examples/rocdown/counter/index.rocdown` puts SQLite helpers in `@roc` next to
`import pf.Sqlite`, then calls them from `@post:command`. `@render` bakes `count: 0`
into the CDN HTML. A full-page `@get:live` app gets generated `GET /sse` on its
`<body>`; a spliced fragment must add
`data-init=@get("/sse", [OpenWhenHidden(True)])` itself. On load, that stream
replaces the snapshot and keeps tabs in sync. Increment and reset are `@post:command` handlers (empty SSE to
Datastar; 204 to `curl`). Opening the CDN file shows the build-time snapshot
until the stream connects.

The public [rocci.dev](/) home page uses the same live pattern, but composes the
standalone [live counter](/examples/live-counter/) app: Markdown plus
`@render LiveCounterUi.CounterIsland(...)`, with
`[http].service` pointing at `LiveCounter.rocci` (handlers + `@get:live`).

`about.rocdown` is `static`. Built `about/index.html` includes hashed `goto.js`
and `script-src 'self'`; it does not include Datastar.

Do not set `[http].service` to `examples/rocci/standalone/counter/Counter.rocci`.
That one-shot app has no `@get:live` stream. A sibling `.rocci` service is allowed
when island routes (commands / live) match what the page posts to; document
`GET /` stays on the CDN.

## Local preview

Debug hybrid sites on the host. Docker is not required for HTML, CSS, or
increment morphing. Use Compose later for Caddy same-origin proxy, published
8001, `ROC_BASIC_WEBSERVER_HOST=0.0.0.0`, and mounted-site path stamps.

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- inspect artifacts examples/rocdown/counter
```

`inspect artifacts` does not invoke Roc. It reports page kinds, Datastar
emission, `service_origin`, and mutation routes. Expect `index` live, `about`
static, and increment/reset POSTs.

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- build examples/rocdown/counter
grep -E 'rd-document|id="counter"|href="/assets/' examples/rocdown/counter/dist/index.html
```

That snapshot check does not start an island process.

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- run examples/rocdown/counter --no-window \
  --output /tmp/rocdown-counter-preview
```

`rocdown view DIR` rebuilds the CDN tree, serves it, and proxies colocated
`/actions/` on the same origin ([http://127.0.0.1:8000](http://127.0.0.1:8000)
with `--no-window`). It logs `preview files at …`. `--output` keeps that tree;
without it the files are temp and deleted on stop. Preview SQLite is
ephemeral. `--no-window` serves in the browser only.

```sh
curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/ | grep -E 'rd-document|#counter|stylesheet'
curl -sf -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/counter/increment \
  -H 'datastar-request: true' -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{}'
```

Open `/`, click Increment, and confirm `#counter output` morphs. Inspector:
[http://127.0.0.1:8000/__rocci/dev](http://127.0.0.1:8000/__rocci/dev). The
complete command list lives in `examples/rocdown/counter/README.md`.

## Build and serve separately

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- build examples/rocdown/counter
cargo run -q -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- serve-islands examples/rocdown/counter --no-window
```

`build` writes the CDN tree (`dist/` in the example). `serve-islands` starts
the mutation process only: `/health` and `/actions/...`. It does not serve
Markdown. Default SQLite path is `{primary}.db` next to the site root (`index.db`
for this example). Set `DB_PATH` to a persistent file in production.

Hashed `/assets/*` files (theme CSS, Datastar.js) are content-addressed and
can be cached indefinitely. HTML, `pages.json`, and `islands.json` should
revalidate.

## Same-origin deploy

Leave `[http].service_origin` empty. The browser POSTs relative `/actions/`
URLs; CSP `connect-src` is `'self'`. Reverse-proxy `/actions/` and `/health`
to `serve-islands`; serve the rest from the CDN tree.

```caddy
example.com {
    handle /actions/* {
        reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8001
    }
    handle /health {
        reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8001
    }
    handle {
        root * /var/www/site
        try_files {path} {path}/index.html
        file_server
    }
}
```

1. `rocdown build` the site.
2. Upload `dist/` to the CDN or object store.
3. Run `rocdown serve-islands` with a persistent `DB_PATH`.
4. Point the reverse proxy at that process for `/actions/` and `/health`.

## Local Docker

Static Rocdown trees (`docs/` in this repository, or any `--cdn-only` `dist/`)
use official Caddy with no Rocci toolchain: build on the host, then
`uv run rocci-ops serve static dist/docs`.

Pre-built hybrid sites package the CDN tree plus an island binary, then
Compose Caddy with a slim process image (no `roc` / `rocdown` at runtime):

```sh
# Match the Linux container CPU (Apple Silicon Docker → arm64musl; amd64 → x64musl)
cargo run -q -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- package examples/rocdown/counter --target arm64musl
uv run rocci-ops serve hybrid examples/rocdown/counter/dist examples/rocdown/counter/islands
```

`--target` follows the **container**, not the Mac host: Apple Silicon local
Docker defaults to `arm64musl`; use `x64musl` only when you also run amd64
images (for example `DOCKER_DEFAULT_PLATFORM=linux/amd64`). Compose does not
auto-select the image arch from `--target`. Do not use `arm64mac` for Linux
images. Operator notes and a short table are in `docker/README.md`.
`uv run rocci-ops serve site` remains the **builder/dev** toolchain demo (Ubuntu +
Roc + WebKit, compile at start), not hosting.

## Cross-origin service

Set an absolute origin and rebuild so action URLs and CSP match:

```toml
[http]
service_origin = "https://islands.example.com"
```

CORS and cookies for that layout are not shipped. Prefer the same-origin
proxy until those details exist.

## Sibling service apps

`[http].service = "Islands.rocci"` skips the generated dispatcher.
`rocdown serve-islands` runs that file with `rocci run`. Routes stay explicit
strings. The app should expose `@get:live` and mutation `@method:command` /
`@method:fragment` handlers the page posts to. Document `GET /` may exist for standalone runs;
the CDN still owns page GET in a hybrid deploy. The rocci.dev home page uses
this shape with `LiveCounter.rocci`.

## Smoke checks

After `build`, the home page HTML includes `#counter` and Datastar; `about/`
does not. With `rocdown view --no-window` on 8000:

```sh
curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
curl -sf -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/counter/increment \
  -H 'datastar-request: true' -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{}'
```

The POST body is a `datastar-patch-elements` event that morphs `#counter`.
`serve-islands` on 8001 is the mutation process alone (no Markdown).

The complete command list lives in `examples/rocdown/counter/README.md`. Handler
syntax is in [Standalone applications](/docs/applications/standalone/).
